<title>USA: Summit gets FDA OK to expand SVS trials.</title>
<headline>Summit gets FDA OK to expand SVS trials.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, MASS. 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summit Technology Inc said Tuesday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration approved the company's plan to expand farsightedness clinical trials using the SVS Apex Plus excimer laser system.</p>
<p>The trials will evaluate the laser's usefulness in correcting mild to moderate farsightedness, the company said.</p>
<p>The company added that it will include results from the trial in a supplemental application it plans to submit to the FDA.</p>
<p>Officials from the company were not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
